@startuml
title Incident lifecycle

[*] --> Open : ticket filed

state "In Progress" as InProgress

Open --> Assigned : on-call solver found\n(automatic on creation,\nor a lead reassigns)
Assigned --> InProgress : solver starts work
InProgress --> Resolved : solver resolves
Resolved --> Closed : solver closes
Resolved --> Open : reopened,\nassigned again automatically
Closed --> Open : reopened,\nassigned again automatically

note right of Open
  A ticket stays Open when the service has
  no team or nobody is on call. The timeline
  records why. It is assigned automatically
  as soon as someone is on call, or a lead
  can hand it over.
end note

note right of Assigned
  The reporter may still edit or delete
  the ticket here. From In Progress on,
  only the assigned solver edits it.
  A team lead may hand it to any other
  solver on the team, here or while
  it is In Progress.
end note

note bottom of Closed
  Every successful transition writes an
  IncidentUpdate row with the user, the
  old state, the new state, and the time.
  Reopening returns the ticket to Open.
  It must then pass through every state
  again in order.
end note

legend right
  |= Rule |= Effect |
  | Skip a state | Refused, message names both states |
  | Go backward | Refused unless reopening from Resolved or Closed |
  | Anyone but the assigned solver or the lead | Refused |
  | Solver off the team | Refused, no access |
  | Open moved by hand | Refused, only assignment leaves Open |
endlegend
@enduml
